values
('math-vector-types-components-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector algebra','Types and components','If a vector A=3i+4j, its magnitude is:','["5","7","12","1"]',0,'|A|=sqrt(3^2+4^2)=5.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-addition-scalar-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector algebra','Addition and scalar multiplication','For a=2i-j and b=i+3j, a+b equals:','["3i+2j","i+2j","3i-4j","2i+3j"]',0,'Add like components: (2+1)i+(-1+3)j=3i+2j.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-section-formula-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector algebra','Section formula','The position vector of the point dividing AB internally in the ratio m:n is:','["(mb+na)/(m+n)","(ma+nb)/(m+n)","(mb-na)/(m+n)","(a+b)/(mn)"]',0,'The internal section formula weights the opposite endpoint vectors, giving (mb+na)/(m+n).','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-linear-combinations-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector algebra','Linear combinations','Vectors a and b are linearly dependent when:','["one is a scalar multiple of the other","their magnitudes are unequal","their dot product is nonzero","both are unit vectors"]',0,'Two vectors are linearly dependent exactly when one is a scalar multiple of the other.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-dot-product-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector products','Dot product','For nonzero vectors a and b with angle theta, a dot b equals:','["|a||b| cos theta","|a||b| sin theta","|a|+|b|","|a||b| tan theta"]',0,'The scalar product is defined as |a||b|cos theta.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-cross-product-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector products','Cross product','The magnitude of a cross b is:','["|a||b| sin theta","|a||b| cos theta","a dot b","|a|+|b|"]',0,'The vector product has magnitude |a||b|sin theta and is perpendicular to both vectors.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-scalar-triple-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector products','Scalar triple product','The absolute value of a dot (b cross c) represents the volume of a:','["parallelepiped","triangle","circle","sphere"]',0,'The scalar triple product gives the signed volume of the parallelepiped formed by the vectors.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-triple-product-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector products','Vector triple product','Which identity is correct?','["a cross (b cross c)=b(a dot c)-c(a dot b)","a cross (b cross c)=a(b dot c)","a cross (b cross c)=c(a dot b)-b(a dot c)","a cross (b cross c)=0 always"]',0,'The BAC-CAB identity is a cross (b cross c)=b(a dot c)-c(a dot b).','advanced',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-geometric-applications-01','mathematics','vectors','Vector products','Geometric applications','The area of a triangle with adjacent side vectors a and b is:','["one-half |a cross b|","|a dot b|","|a cross b|","two |a cross b|"]',0,'|a cross b| is the parallelogram area, so the triangle area is half of it.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-line-equation-01','mathematics','vectors','Lines and planes','Vector equation of a line','A line through position vector a and parallel to vector b is:','["r=a+lambda b","r=lambda a+b","r=a dot b","r=a cross b"]',0,'Every point is reached from a by a scalar displacement along b.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-plane-equation-01','mathematics','vectors','Lines and planes','Vector equation of a plane','A plane through position vector a with normal n satisfies:','["(r-a) dot n=0","(r-a) cross n=0","r=a+lambda n","r dot a=0"]',0,'Every in-plane displacement r-a is perpendicular to the normal n.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-coplanarity-01','mathematics','vectors','Lines and planes','Coplanarity','Three vectors a,b,c are coplanar when:','["a dot (b cross c)=0","a dot b=0","a cross b=0 always","their magnitudes are equal"]',0,'Zero scalar triple product means the parallelepiped volume is zero, hence the vectors are coplanar.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-vector-skew-shortest-01','mathematics','vectors','Lines and planes','Skew lines and shortest distance','For skew lines with direction vectors b1,b2 and points a1,a2, the shortest distance is:','["|(a2-a1) dot (b1 cross b2)|/|b1 cross b2|","|(a2-a1) dot b1|/|b1|","|b1 cross b2|","|(a2-a1) cross b1|"]',0,'Project the connector onto the common-normal direction b1 cross b2.','advanced',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-sample-events-01','mathematics','probability','Probability foundations','Sample spaces and events','An event in a random experiment is:','["a subset of the sample space","always one outcome","the probability value itself","a repeated trial only"]',0,'The sample space contains all outcomes and an event is any specified subset.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI-XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-classical-axiomatic-01','mathematics','probability','Probability foundations','Classical and axiomatic probability','Which axiom is valid for every event A?','["0 <= P(A) <= 1","P(A)>1","P(A)<0","P(A)=1 always"]',0,'Probability is nonnegative and cannot exceed one.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI-XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-addition-01','mathematics','probability','Probability foundations','Addition theorem','For any events A and B, P(A union B) equals:','["P(A)+P(B)-P(A intersection B)","P(A)+P(B)","P(A)P(B)","P(A)-P(B)"]',0,'Subtract the intersection once because it is included in both individual probabilities.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI-XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-complement-01','mathematics','probability','Probability foundations','Complementary events','For event A, P(not A) is:','["1-P(A)","1+P(A)","P(A)","0 always"]',0,'A and its complement are disjoint and exhaust the sample space.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI-XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-multiplication-01','mathematics','probability','Conditional probability','Multiplication theorem','If P(A)>0, then P(A intersection B) equals:','["P(A)P(B|A)","P(A)+P(B|A)","P(A)/P(B|A)","P(B)-P(A)"]',0,'This is the multiplication rule obtained from the definition of conditional probability.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-independent-01','mathematics','probability','Conditional probability','Independent events','Events A and B are independent when:','["P(A intersection B)=P(A)P(B)","P(A union B)=0","P(A)=P(B)","A and B are disjoint always"]',0,'Independence means the occurrence of one does not change the probability of the other.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-total-01','mathematics','probability','Conditional probability','Total probability','If B1,...,Bn partition the sample space, P(A) equals:','["sum P(Bi)P(A|Bi)","sum P(A)P(Bi|A)","product P(Bi)","1-P(A)"]',0,'Split A across the mutually exclusive and exhaustive cases Bi, then add their probabilities.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-bayes-01','mathematics','probability','Conditional probability','Bayes theorem','Bayes theorem is chiefly used to:','["reverse a conditional probability using prior information","add mutually exclusive events","find a vector magnitude","differentiate a function"]',0,'Bayes theorem updates prior probabilities and reverses the conditioning direction.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-discrete-rv-01','mathematics','probability','Random variables','Discrete random variables','A discrete random variable takes:','["a countable set of values","every real value in an interval","no numerical values","only negative values"]',0,'Discrete variables have finite or countably infinite possible values.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-distributions-01','mathematics','probability','Random variables','Probability distributions','For a discrete probability distribution, the sum of all probabilities is:','["1","0","the mean","the variance"]',0,'The listed outcomes exhaust the sample space, so their probabilities sum to one.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-expectation-variance-01','mathematics','probability','Random variables','Expectation and variance','For a random variable X, Var(X) equals:','["E(X^2)-[E(X)]^2","E(X^2)+[E(X)]^2","E(X)^2","E(X)-E(X^2)"]',0,'Expanding E[(X-E(X))^2] gives E(X^2)-[E(X)]^2.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-binomial-01','mathematics','probability','Random variables','Binomial distribution','For X~Bin(n,p), the mean is:','["np","n+p","np(1-p)","p/n"]',0,'A binomial variable is the sum of n independent Bernoulli variables, each with mean p.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XII; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-probability-poisson-01','mathematics','probability','Random variables','Poisson distribution','For a Poisson distribution with parameter lambda, mean and variance are:','["both lambda","lambda and lambda squared","both one","lambda squared and lambda"]',0,'A defining property of the Poisson distribution is E(X)=Var(X)=lambda.','standard',array['tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','State-board Intermediate Mathematics; official EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
